 "_about": "The word list the Romanian course is measured against (Builder 2, 2026-11-21, branch content/ro-a1). No free CEFR-graded Romanian A1 inventory exists (no Kelly list; the nearest, Arieșan-Simion's Inventarul lexical al limbii române ca limbă străină, nivel A1, is copyright and not published as data), so this is a FREQUENCY stand-in, as the Dutch, Danish and Norwegian courses use: the 1000 most frequent Romanian surface forms from the hermitdave FrequencyWords list (OpenSubtitles 2018, CC BY-SA 4.0), in frequency order, headwords only. Prepared from the source: the old cedilla letters ş ţ folded to comma-below ș ț (counts merged), and a diacritic-less subtitle spelling dropped where the same word with its diacritics ranks higher (sa for să, si for și, asa for așa, daca for dacă). Frequency is not CEFR, so the top ranks hold pronouns, particles and spoken fillers more than a syllabus list would. Core target (as French uses FLELex 600): the 600 most frequent.",
